@startuml
!include theme.iuml
title Option desk - One source of truth for four runtimes

component "shell/skills/*/SKILL.md\n6 skills, each carrying the\nreporting rules an agent must\nfollow, not just the commands" as skill #C6E9C6
component "shell/tools/gen_runtime_docs.py\nreads skills + argparse parsers" as gen
component "AGENTS.md (4,366 bytes)\nrules + command inventory for Codex,\nwhich loads skills itself\nfrom .agents/skills" as agents
component "GEMINI.md\nthe same plus all six skills\ncompiled in: Gemini CLI\ndiscovers none" as gemini
component "Claude Code\nreads SKILL.md directly\n(plugin adds commands + agents)" as claude
component "optiondesk-mcp\n10 typed tool schemas:\nbetter than prose describing\na command line" as mcpserver

skill --> gen : generate
gen --> agents
gen --> gemini
skill --> claude : read as-is
skill ..> mcpserver : same capabilities,\ntyped instead of prose
mcpserver --> claude
mcpserver --> agents
mcpserver --> gemini

note right of gen
Two tests guard this:
- generated text vs what is on disk:
  a stale AGENTS.md fails the suite
- every argparse subcommand must
  appear in both copies: a command
  added without documentation fails
end note

note bottom of agents
Embedding all skills in AGENTS.md
took it to 25,851 bytes and defeated
progressive disclosure. Naming where
they live instead: 4,366 bytes.
end note

caption Edit a skill, run the generator, and every runtime gets the change in the same commit.
@enduml
